          "id": "sec-2-7",
          "secNumber": "2.7",
          "heading": "Integrated civil case study",
          "content": "## Integrated civil case study\n\nBridge-deck support audit: derive reactions for a simplified span with two point actions and a continuous self-weight. Test whether each proposed support can deliver its modeled action and document missing settlement or uplift information.\n\n\n### Worked problem studio\n\nEach problem below is a separate numerical case. Work it first without looking at the answer, then compare the force and moment checks. Changing dimensions can reveal near-singular geometry or support reactions that switch direction.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.1\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 4.0 m beam carries 1.50 kN/m across the span and a 5.0 kN point load at x=0.80 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=6.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=4.000 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=7.000 kN. Check RA+RB=11.000 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.2\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 4.5 m beam carries 1.75 kN/m across the span and a 6.3 kN point load at x=1.12 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=7.875 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=5.513 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=8.662 kN. Check RA+RB=14.175 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.3\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 5.0 m beam carries 2.00 kN/m across the span and a 7.6 kN point load at x=1.50 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=10.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=7.280 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=10.320 kN. Check RA+RB=17.600 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.4\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 5.5 m beam carries 2.25 kN/m across the span and a 8.9 kN point load at x=1.93 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=12.375 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=9.303 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=11.973 kN. Check RA+RB=21.275 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.5\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 6.0 m beam carries 2.50 kN/m across the span and a 10.2 kN point load at x=2.40 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=15.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=11.580 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=13.620 kN. Check RA+RB=25.200 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.6\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 6.5 m beam carries 2.75 kN/m across the span and a 11.5 kN point load at x=2.93 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=17.875 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=14.113 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=15.262 kN. Check RA+RB=29.375 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.7\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 7.0 m beam carries 3.00 kN/m across the span and a 12.8 kN point load at x=3.50 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=21.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=16.900 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=16.900 kN. Check RA+RB=33.800 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.8\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 7.5 m beam carries 3.25 kN/m across the span and a 14.1 kN point load at x=4.12 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=24.375 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=19.942 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=18.532 kN. Check RA+RB=38.475 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.9\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 8.0 m beam carries 3.50 kN/m across the span and a 15.4 kN point load at x=4.80 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=28.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=23.240 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=20.160 kN. Check RA+RB=43.400 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.10\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 8.5 m beam carries 3.75 kN/m across the span and a 16.7 kN point load at x=1.70 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=31.875 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=19.277 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=29.297 kN. Check RA+RB=48.575 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.11\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 9.0 m beam carries 4.00 kN/m across the span and a 18.0 kN point load at x=2.25 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=36.000 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=22.500 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=31.500 kN. Check RA+RB=54.000 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis.\n\n\n#### Worked problem 2.12\n\n**Given:** A simply supported 9.5 m beam carries 4.25 kN/m across the span and a 19.3 kN point load at x=2.85 m. Determine end reactions.\n\n**Solution:** Uniform action = wL=40.375 kN at L/2. Taking moments about A yields RB=wL/2+Pa/L=25.977 kN. Vertical balance gives RA=wL/2+P(L\u2212a)/L=33.697 kN. Check RA+RB=59.675 kN matches wL+P.\n\n**Review check:** State the units and verify whether the result reflects the applied load path. Identify one assumption whose failure would require a new analysis."
