          "content": "Geometric section properties condense cross-sectional geometry into quantities useful for stress and stiffness calculations. At the statics stage they mainly provide distributed-load centroids and axes for follow-on mechanics-of-materials work. A centroid is an area-weighted location: for a homogeneous plate of uniform thickness it matches its center of mass, but for layered materials it does not necessarily locate the mass center. The second moment of area is a fourth-power geometric property, not a physical mass moment of inertia.\n\n**Engineering boundary:** These exercises analyze idealized statics models for education. They do **not** certify structural strength, earthquake/wind resistance, geotechnical bearing, connection design, construction safety, or compliance with any jurisdiction\u2019s building code. Real works require local standards, authoritative loading data and qualified professional checking."
