          "heading": "Unit assessment (with guidance)",
          "content": "## Unit assessment (with guidance)\n\n**Q1.** Find the centroidal height of an inverted T composed of two non-overlapping rectangles. Specify datum.\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 5; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q2.** A 120 mm \u00d7 220 mm rectangle is rotated by 90\u00b0. How do its centroidal second moments change?\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 5; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q3.** Why is a centroidal area second moment measured in mm\u2074 rather than mm\u00b2?\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 5; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q4.** Explain when a geometric centroid is not the center of mass of a composite member.\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 5; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone."
