          "heading": "Theoretical Framework: Friction, Sliding, Overturning and Stability",
          "content": "Foundation contact and retaining systems can fail by sliding, overturning, loss of bearing contact or internal structural distress. These mechanisms are different; passing one check does not prove the system safe. A rigid-body sliding calculation is governed by the maximum friction or other available resistance, whereas overturning depends on the relative location of stabilizing and destabilizing resultants. Soil\u2013structure interaction, groundwater, passive pressure, anchorage and applicable factors require specialist treatment beyond introductory statics.\n\n**Engineering boundary:** These exercises analyze idealized statics models for education. They do **not** certify structural strength, earthquake/wind resistance, geotechnical bearing, connection design, construction safety, or compliance with any jurisdiction\u2019s building code. Real works require local standards, authoritative loading data and qualified professional checking."
