          "heading": "Unit assessment (with guidance)",
          "content": "## Unit assessment (with guidance)\n\n**Q1.** Explain why static friction does not always equal \u03bcN.\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 6; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q2.** With W=75 kN and \u03bc=0.4, calculate ideal maximum base friction. What information is still missing for design?\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 6; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q3.** A wall has 100 kN weight over a 2 m base and 25 kN lateral action at 3 m. Compare opposing toe moments.\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 6; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone.\n\n**Q4.** Why does a positive nominal overturning ratio not prove satisfactory soil bearing pressure?\n\n*Guidance:* Use the governing equation and a labeled diagram from Unit 6; report direction, magnitude, units and model assumptions. Numerical assessment answers should be obtained from the worked methods, not from inspection of figures alone."
